media: h713-hdmirx: the driver's remaining German messages, in English

Every line this driver has added since 0136f is English, but the strings it
started with are German, so a boot log reads in two languages and a user who
does not speak one of them gets half a message. T2's report (section 8.2)
names them and leaves them alone on purpose - they belong in a patch of
their own rather than folded into a change that does something else.

Translated, same meaning, no behaviour change:

  - the INCAP rowbyte fallback warning in h713_hdmirx_ring_geometry(),
  - "INCAP reports no geometry" in h713_hdmirx_detect_timings(),
  - the signal-info bounds warning in h713_hdmirx_read_signal_info(),
  - every dev_err_probe()/dev_warn()/dev_info() string of probe() and of the
    two helpers it calls (h713_hdmirx_get_region, h713_hdmirx_check_ring),
  - the two struct h713_hdmirx member comments T2 names.

Twenty-one lines, all of them string literals or comments; the code around
them is untouched and checkpatch counts the same 0 errors / 25 warnings as
before.

What this patch does NOT translate, and a correction: T2 8.2 calls the
German strings "five places". They are not. After this patch a German-word
scan over the file still names sixty-three lines: the whole release path
(h713_hdmirx_rearm and its two work handlers, every "Freigabe:" line), the
colour-converter path ("Farbwandler:"), the init-sequence lines, the
bring-up value line, the saturation warning, the streaming summary, the open
refusal, and all of the debugfs status file. They are user-visible too and
want exactly the same treatment. They are left out here because the scope of
this patch is the list T2 names, because sixty-three more lines is a patch
of a different size, and because the status file's wording changes again in
0136n and 0136m - so translating it twice would be wasted work. The full
line list is in umbau/work/Q3/REPORT.txt.

Source: umbau/work/T2/REPORT.txt section 8.2, doku/128 section 3 item 3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

